    "summary": "Dark Star odyssey with soaring Mountains of the Moon and soulful Rag",
    "blurb": "The show delivers an extended Dark Star that rides a high‑energy wave, punctuated by a standout rendition of Doin' That Rag and a haunting Death Don't Have No Mercy. Jerry Garcia’s vocals and lead work are front‑and‑center, while Mountains Of The Moon adds a delicate acoustic lift.",
    "review": "April 20, 1969 at Atwood Hall captures the Dead in a pivotal early‑psychedelic phase. After opening with Morning Dew and Good Morning Little School Girl, the band launches into a mesmerizing Dark Star that feels both exploratory and tightly knit—Jerry’s tone on fire, Phil’s bass anchoring every twist. The momentum rolls through Saint Stephen and The Eleven before landing on a deeply felt Death Don't Have No Mercy. Doin' That Rag showcases Garcia’s gritty vocals and spirited soloing, while the encore’s Dupree's Diamond Blues segues into a soaring Mountains Of The Moon that offers a gentle, almost reverent contrast to the earlier jams. Though the primary soundboard source bears some hiss and low volume, its completeness and the raw intensity of the performances make it the go‑to recording for this historic night.",
